  clock: 3  # ddac
  nonce: ddac  # ddac
  message: "Fixed in PR #598 (selfh dev 766e813290). Python display Symbol.signature now renders real default values (bounded per value; over-long/unparseable -> ellipsis) and uses a 240-char cap with graceful truncation that preserves the return type, instead of a bare =ellipsis for every default + a 60-char blind mid-content cut. STRUCTURAL: the display signature also feeds normalize_python_signature -> make_typed_stable_id (normalize keeps default values AND truncation flips typed->untyped), so a naive widening would have churned every Python stable_id (verified empirically). Decoupled: _format_function_signature gains render_defaults + wide max_len used ONLY for the display field; the stable_id/normalize input keeps the byte-identical legacy 60-char/=ellipsis form -> zero identity churn. 6 tests (4 updated incl a decoupling assertion, 2 added); spec nodes[] signature field documented. Wave-5 P1."  # ddac
